4	//! Prometheus metrics for the KV router.
5	//!
6	//! This module centralizes all router-side Prometheus metric definitions:
7	//!
8	//! - [`WorkerLoadMetrics`]: Per-worker active decode blocks and prefill tokens gauges.
9	//!   Registered on the frontend's own `prometheus::Registry` (default port 8000).
10	//!   Populated by `KvWorkerMonitor` in the frontend when receiving ActiveLoad events.
11	//!   - Frontend (aggregated and disaggregated): available on default port 8000
12	//!   - Standalone router (`python -m dynamo.router`): not created (frontend-only)
13	//!
14	//! - [`RoutingOverheadMetrics`]: Per-request routing phase latency histograms.
15	//!   Registered on the frontend's own `prometheus::Registry` (default port 8000).
16	//!   Populated by `RoutingHost` in the frontend during routing decisions.
17	//!   - Frontend (aggregated and disaggregated): available on default port 8000
18	//!   - Standalone router: not created (frontend-only)
19	//!
20	//! - [`RouterRequestMetrics`]: Per-request aggregate histograms and counters (TTFT, ITL,
21	//!   tokens, KV hit rate, and non-max-overlap routing decisions).
22	//!   Registered on the DRT `MetricsRegistry` hierarchy via `Component::metrics()`.
23	//!   Eagerly created so they appear as zeros before any requests arrive.
24	//!   Populated by `RoutingHost::generate()` and its `RequestGuard` as it observes
25	//!   the streaming response (TTFT on first token, ITL per output block,
26	//!   ISL/OSL/kv_hit_rate at routing and completion).
27	//!   - Frontend, builtin modes without affinity or LoRA filtering: populated by `RoutingHost`;
28	//!     modes that still bypass the host remain registered as zeros
29	//!   - Frontend, KV mode (aggregated and disaggregated): available on default port
30	//!     8000 via the `drt_metrics` bridge, populated per-request
31	//!   - Standalone router (`python -m dynamo.router`): available on `DYN_SYSTEM_PORT`
32	//!     when set (default is `-1`, disabled), populated per-request
33	//!
34	//! - `KvPublisherMetrics`: Worker-local KV event publisher and ZMQ relay counters.
35	//!   Registered on the DRT `MetricsRegistry` hierarchy via `Component::metrics()`.
36	//!   Populated by `KvEventPublisher` and the ZMQ listener when engines publish KV
37	//!   events.
38	//!
39	//! The standalone router does not create `WorkerLoadMetrics` or
40	//! `RoutingOverheadMetrics` (those are frontend-only). It only exposes
41	//! `RouterRequestMetrics` and standard DRT transport metrics
42	//! (`dynamo_component_inflight_requests`, `dynamo_component_requests_total`, etc.)
43	//! via the system status server when `DYN_SYSTEM_PORT` is explicitly set.
44	//!
45	//! See also: `docs/observability/metrics.md` (Router Metrics section).
