805	/// Aggregate per-request metrics observed at the router level.
806	///
807	/// Component-scoped via `from_component()` to get automatic `dynamo_component_` prefix,
808	/// `dynamo_namespace`/`dynamo_component`/`dynamo_endpoint` labels, and registration
809	/// with the DRT `MetricsRegistry` hierarchy.
810	///
811	/// # Scrapeability
812	///
813	/// - **Frontend, non-KV modes**: Always zero (registered but never populated).
814	/// - **Frontend, KV mode (aggregated and disaggregated)**: Available on the
815	///   frontend's `/metrics` endpoint (default port 8000) via the `drt_metrics`
816	///   bridge, populated per-request.
817	/// - **Standalone router** (`python -m dynamo.router`): Available on the system
818	///   status server when `DYN_SYSTEM_PORT` is set, populated per-request.
819	///
820	/// # When these metrics are created
821	///
822	/// Eagerly in `RoutingHost::new()`, so they appear as zeros before any requests.
823	/// Both the frontend pipeline and the standalone router (via Python bindings)
824	/// create a `RoutingHost`, so both get these metrics registered automatically.
825	///
826	/// # Why component-scoped
827	///
828	/// These metrics MUST be registered through the Component hierarchy (not a standalone
829	/// registry). In global planner deployments, the frontend's router is the global
830	/// entry point, but each worker pool has its own local router (e.g. prefill pool,
831	/// decode pool). Component-scoped metrics let each local router emit metrics with
832	/// distinct `dynamo_component` labels, so pools can be monitored and scaled
833	/// independently.
